1
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:46,710
We're riding towards Absolution.

2
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,160
You know how far west we are?

3
00:03:57,970 --> 00:03:59,700
Maybe he's a dummy.

4
00:04:00,270 --> 00:04:03,200
Is there a reason
you're not answering my question?

5
00:04:03,970 --> 00:04:07,030
Look here, Pa.
He's got iron on his wrist.

6
00:04:07,140 --> 00:04:09,170
He's been shot.

7
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,770
Could be he done
broke out of the hoosegow.

8
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:13,240
Might be worth bounty money.

9
00:04:13,350 --> 00:04:14,870
Might could be.

10
00:04:22,890 --> 00:04:25,450
It's not your lucky day, stranger.

11
00:04:26,890 --> 00:04:28,160
Turn around and start walking.

12
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,560
I said turn around and start walking!

13
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,140
Get out.

14
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,500
Hello?

15
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:59,390
Palms to heaven, friend.

16
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:01,730
Easy now.

17
00:09:08,110 --> 00:09:12,170
All right. Turn around, nice and slow.

18
00:09:12,650 --> 00:09:14,140
I've been shot.

19
00:09:21,020 --> 00:09:24,580
Only two kinds of men get shot,
criminals and victims.

20
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:27,930
Which one are you?

21
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:30,690
I don't know.

22
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:32,690
You got a name, friend?

23
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,870
I don't know that either.

24
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:38,130
Just what do you know?

25
00:09:39,470 --> 00:09:40,840
English.

26
00:09:48,450 --> 00:09:52,220
Well, that is a right odd-looking
wound there.

27
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:56,250
Looks almost cauterized.

28
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:59,790
All right, this might sting a bit.

29
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:03,920
Is this a mining town?

30
00:10:06,970 --> 00:10:10,600
Yeah. Well, that was the notion.

31
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:15,680
People moved on, though. No gold.

32
00:10:15,810 --> 00:10:17,970
All right now, try and hold still.

33
00:10:21,650 --> 00:10:23,140
There we go.

34
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:26,520
This is no gunshot.

35
00:10:27,220 --> 00:10:28,550
Where'd you get this, son?

36
00:10:28,660 --> 00:10:30,090
I don't know.

37
00:10:30,190 --> 00:10:34,220
I can't rightly absolve you of your sins
if you don't recall 'em, can I?

38
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:38,490
That being said,
I've seen good men do bad things

39
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:40,900
and bad men do good things.

40
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:44,570
Whether you're gonna
end up in heaven or hell,

41
00:10:44,670 --> 00:10:47,300
it's not God's plan, it's your own.

42
00:10:48,110 --> 00:10:50,740
You just got to remember what it was.

43
00:10:50,850 --> 00:10:52,780
All right, put me a finger right here.

44
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:54,070
Come on.

45
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:55,810
There you go.

46
00:11:00,290 --> 00:11:01,620
There.

47
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:04,050
Thank you.

48
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:06,130
Not bad for a country preacher.

49
00:11:12,930 --> 00:11:14,960
It's that damn fool Dolarhyde kid.

50
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,700
Hey! What are you doing?

51
00:11:18,810 --> 00:11:20,900
What are you doing, Percy?
There's people up there!

52
00:11:21,010 --> 00:11:22,500
There's no one up there. It's fine.

53
00:11:22,610 --> 00:11:24,840
It's not fine.
It's bad enough he drinks for free.

54
00:11:24,950 --> 00:11:27,110
Now he's got to shoot up the place?

55
00:11:27,210 --> 00:11:28,440
Wait, what was that, Doc?

56
00:11:28,550 --> 00:11:30,520
Nothing. He didn't say anything.
Everything's okay.

57
00:11:30,620 --> 00:11:31,880
Please go back inside.

58
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:33,110
Shut up.

59
00:11:35,290 --> 00:11:39,160
I want to hear what you said.
"It's bad enough" what?

60
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:43,660
You ungrateful for our business?

61
00:11:44,130 --> 00:11:46,290
'Cause if it wasn't for my pa's cattle,

62
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:48,490
there'd be no money
going through this town!

63
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:53,270
There'd be no meat on your tables!
And your doors would be closed!

64
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:57,970
I don't mean no disrespect
to your father, Percy. You know that.

65
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:01,740
Of course not.
But you ask me to pay.

66
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:04,880
Come here, let's settle up.

67
00:12:06,850 --> 00:12:08,120
Come here.

68
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:14,930
Hey.

69
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:18,390
Hey, kid, I don't want any trouble.
I'm just trying to...

70
00:12:20,530 --> 00:12:24,940
Better pick up your glasses, Doc,
before someone steps on them.

71
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:32,210
Stop!

72
00:12:32,310 --> 00:12:33,710
I'll pay the goddamn bill!

73
00:12:34,010 --> 00:12:38,680
All right, son! We're just trying
to make a living now. Come on.

74
00:12:38,790 --> 00:12:42,520
You know what, preacher?
You just gave me an idea.

75
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:45,350
I know it ain't Sunday, folks,

76
00:12:45,490 --> 00:12:48,990
but what say we take up
a collection for the poor man?

77
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:52,330
Now, who's got money?

78
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,770
In the hat.

79
00:12:56,070 --> 00:12:57,590
Let's go.

80
00:12:57,710 --> 00:12:59,330
Much obliged.

81
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:01,430
Now, I'm sorry Doc's bad fortune

82
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:04,200
has to be taken out on you good people.
In the hat.

83
00:13:05,310 --> 00:13:07,250
That's mighty Christian of you.

84
00:13:11,650 --> 00:13:12,620
Hey.

85
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,290
You, too.

86
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:20,250
You want to be careful where you point
that thing before you get hurt.

87
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,270
Listen...

88
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:35,540
I'm gonna give you
the benefit of the doubt, because

89
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:38,880
maybe you don't know who I am.

90
00:13:52,130 --> 00:13:54,290
- Come on.
- Get off of me!

91
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:55,690
Hey, you!

92
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:59,460
I'm warning you.

93
00:14:11,610 --> 00:14:13,170
Are you all right?

94
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:14,770
Where the hell did he come from?

95
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:17,750
Where the hell did he come from?

96
00:14:17,850 --> 00:14:19,840
What the hell is going on here?

97
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:24,780
It was an accident.
He came out of nowhere.

98
00:14:24,890 --> 00:14:28,850
And he dry-gulched me.
He tried to make me look like a fool.

99
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,760
It wasn't my fault, Sheriff.

100
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:34,560
Damn it, Percy. You crossed the line
this time. I gotta lock you up.

101
00:14:34,670 --> 00:14:35,900
Taggart.

102
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:38,900
You know that's not a good idea.

103
00:14:39,510 --> 00:14:42,500
Well, I'm afraid I got no choice, Nat.

104
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:46,040
Nat?

105
00:14:46,810 --> 00:14:49,410
Nat, you son of a bitch,
where you going?

106
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:54,540
Don't worry. I'll tell your father
about what happened today.

107
00:14:58,830 --> 00:15:01,020
You burned the coffee again, Mickey.

108
00:15:01,130 --> 00:15:04,360
Well. Tell you what, Ed.
Next time, you can make the coffee.

109
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:05,560
- Okay.
- All right.

110
00:15:05,670 --> 00:15:08,070
Why don't you take it easy
on that Taos Lightnin', Murphy?

111
00:15:08,170 --> 00:15:10,300
Mr. Dolarhyde
don't like drinking on the job.

112
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:13,810
Mr. Dolarhyde
don't like drinking on the job?

113
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:20,640
I don't give a rat's ass what the high
and mighty Colonel Dolarhyde don't like!

114
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:24,810
I don't care how many Indians
he put under neither.

115
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:27,620
You sure do flap your gums a lot
when the boss ain't around.

116
00:15:32,690 --> 00:15:35,390
I'd say it to his face if he was here!

117
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:38,370
Colonel Dolarhyde.

118
00:15:44,370 --> 00:15:47,340
I'm gonna tell you something, boys.

119
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:51,300
Money makes you soft.

120
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:29,880
Where the hell's that coach?

121
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:32,410
Coach? What coach?

122
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:34,490
You shot a deputy, Percy.

123
00:16:35,090 --> 00:16:37,580
Federal Marshal's
bringing you to Santa Fe.

124
00:16:37,690 --> 00:16:39,420
Federal Marshal?

125
00:16:39,530 --> 00:16:41,890
Sheriff, have you lost your mind?

126
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:44,790
My pa is on his way down here.

127
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:47,990
You better let me out of here
before things get out of hand.

128
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:53,800
Sheriff, it was an accident!
It's not like I'm Jesse James!

129
00:16:54,040 --> 00:16:55,570
Son of a bitch.

130
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:00,610
Could you put that on Percy's tab?

131
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,510
Fifty cents.

132
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:05,840
Just kidding with you, there, Doc.

133
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:12,360
I got no respect in this town.

134
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:14,090
That's not true, okay?

135
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:16,790
You want to leave?

136
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:20,630
No. This is your dream.
I'd follow you anywhere.

137
00:17:20,730 --> 00:17:21,960
I thought it was our dream.

138
00:17:24,070 --> 00:17:25,800
God damn it!

139
00:17:25,910 --> 00:17:28,100
Hey, Charlie,
why don't you play something festive?

140
00:17:28,210 --> 00:17:30,340
It's like a funeral in here!

141
00:17:36,250 --> 00:17:39,480
Hey, you don't have
to prove anything, okay?

142
00:17:39,590 --> 00:17:41,820
Okay? I love you.

143
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:43,510
I'm not a child.

144
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,670
Whiskey.

145
00:18:04,510 --> 00:18:07,040
On the house, for what you did.

146
00:18:26,470 --> 00:18:28,260
I'm just here to drink.

147
00:18:33,810 --> 00:18:36,000
- Do I know you?
- No.

148
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:43,250
My name's Ella.

149
00:18:46,490 --> 00:18:48,960
Where'd you get your bracelet?

150
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:54,420
There something you know about me,
lady?

151
00:18:55,730 --> 00:18:58,160
You don't remember anything, do you?

152
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:03,740
What do you want?

153
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:06,430
I know you're looking for something.

154
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:07,840
So am I.

155
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:11,800
Well, good luck to you.

156
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:21,850
Move away.

157
00:19:30,830 --> 00:19:32,460
Jake Lonergan.

158
00:19:52,090 --> 00:19:54,490
You mind following me
over to the office,

159
00:19:54,590 --> 00:19:56,520
so we can have us a little chat?

160
00:19:59,930 --> 00:20:02,230
I think you've got the wrong man.

161
00:20:04,770 --> 00:20:07,560
Well, I'm gonna need you
to come with us all the same.

162
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:12,570
Wouldn't do that if I was you.

163
00:20:40,070 --> 00:20:41,300
No!

164
00:20:44,570 --> 00:20:46,540
I don't want any trouble.

165
00:21:30,050 --> 00:21:31,750
Rise and shine.

166
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:38,010
You're in trouble now.

167
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:40,250
You're gonna burn.

168
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:42,490
My pa is coming for me.

169
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:48,530
He learned how to kill a man
good and slow in the war.

170
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:51,570
I am going to watch you suffer

171
00:21:51,670 --> 00:21:54,000
for a long,

172
00:21:54,110 --> 00:21:55,570
long,

173
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,840
long time.

174
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:03,680
You thought
that cheap shot in the pecker hurt?

175
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:15,130
Please! I didn't kill your cattle.

176
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:19,030
Colonel Dolarhyde.
You got to believe me!

177
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:25,130
You only been riding for my brand
for what, two weeks?

178
00:22:27,340 --> 00:22:30,500
You don't maybe know
who you're dealing with, Roy.

179
00:22:34,350 --> 00:22:36,480
Nobody calls me "Colonel."

180
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:40,080
Them that did are mostly dead.

181
00:22:43,790 --> 00:22:45,090
Please.

182
00:22:47,030 --> 00:22:50,830
So you, Ed and Little Mickey is picking
up strays. How many did you get?

183
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:53,360
Got 24 of 'em, boss.

184
00:22:53,470 --> 00:22:56,030
You been drinking, ain't you?
I can smell it on you.

185
00:22:56,140 --> 00:22:59,260
I haven't been drinking none.
It's them other two's that drinked.

186
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:03,940
What kind of a man goes around
blowing up other people's cows

187
00:23:04,040 --> 00:23:08,540
then tells a bullshit story like this?
You couldn't do no better?

188
00:23:08,650 --> 00:23:11,080
You got to believe me.
There was white lights!

189
00:23:11,220 --> 00:23:12,550
There was bright lights!

190
00:23:12,650 --> 00:23:16,610
So there was this big light,
and you fell in the river

191
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:18,160
and when you come back,

192
00:23:18,260 --> 00:23:20,850
two of my best hands
has just disappeared.

193
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:27,960
There weren't no storm.
There weren't no lightning this evening.

194
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:30,130
You don't respect me, do you, Roy?

195
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:31,300
Boss!

196
00:23:34,840 --> 00:23:36,600
Where's Percy?

197
00:23:36,710 --> 00:23:38,540
Taggart locked him up, boss.

198
00:23:38,650 --> 00:23:41,340
Why? What'd he do now?

199
00:23:41,750 --> 00:23:43,270
Shot a deputy.

200
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:45,210
God damn it!

201
00:23:45,320 --> 00:23:48,150
What the hell
does Taggart think he's doing?

202
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:50,310
He wouldn't even have a job if I...

203
00:23:50,420 --> 00:23:53,420
Now I got to go in there
and reason with him!

204
00:23:53,530 --> 00:23:56,500
'Cause you failed to look after my boy!

205
00:24:01,030 --> 00:24:03,160
Thank you. Thank you.

206
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:08,000
All right. Everybody, saddle up.

207
00:24:12,980 --> 00:24:15,610
Boss, we ought to get more hands.

208
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:16,770
Why?

209
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:21,120
You're not gonna believe this,
but I think Jake Lonergan's in town.

210
00:24:32,570 --> 00:24:35,260
I'm turning you over
to the Federal Marshal.

211
00:24:37,300 --> 00:24:39,030
You're gonna tell me
what I am charged with?

212
00:24:41,740 --> 00:24:44,470
Arson. Assault.

213
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:46,670
Mayhem. Hijacking.

214
00:24:48,980 --> 00:24:53,480
It says you robbed the stage last month
with Pat Dolan and Bull McCade.

215
00:24:54,150 --> 00:24:56,880
Which makes you
accessory to every law they broke, too.

216
00:25:03,230 --> 00:25:04,290
That it?

217
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:06,630
Murder.

218
00:25:07,770 --> 00:25:11,070
Prostitute out of Cottonwood Grove,
next county over.

219
00:25:11,170 --> 00:25:13,140
Name of Alice Wills.

220
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:17,440
You saying I killed this woman?

221
00:25:17,780 --> 00:25:19,540
You tell me.

222
00:26:03,820 --> 00:26:05,090
Damn.

223
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:10,080
Give me your wrist.

224
00:26:11,360 --> 00:26:12,760
Taggart, what are you doing?

225
00:26:14,330 --> 00:26:15,360
Sheriff.

226
00:26:16,540 --> 00:26:19,000
Sheriff, this is going too far.

227
00:26:19,970 --> 00:26:21,340
I was just fooling around.

228
00:26:23,310 --> 00:26:25,370
Look, I didn't mean to hurt anybody.

229
00:26:25,810 --> 00:26:27,010
Go away.

230
00:26:27,110 --> 00:26:31,110
Listen, I'm sorry, but I had no choice.
I couldn't let you leave.

231
00:26:31,220 --> 00:26:33,240
Well, I'm leaving now.

232
00:26:33,890 --> 00:26:35,120
I need you.

233
00:26:35,220 --> 00:26:37,280
You got something to say, say it.

234
00:26:38,830 --> 00:26:41,320
I need to know where you came from.

235
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:43,660
So do I.

236
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:47,170
Ma'am.

237
00:26:53,170 --> 00:26:55,140
You two lovebirds have a nice trip now.

238
00:26:57,740 --> 00:27:00,710
Taggart! Taggart, let me out of here!

239
00:27:01,410 --> 00:27:02,610
Sheriff!

240
00:27:03,680 --> 00:27:04,950
Sheriff!

241
00:27:05,790 --> 00:27:06,810
What are you doing?

242
00:27:08,890 --> 00:27:10,720
You get back home. Go to bed.

243
00:27:10,820 --> 00:27:12,790
Please don't go.

244
00:27:12,890 --> 00:27:15,790
I have to, Emmett. It's my job.

245
00:27:16,130 --> 00:27:17,690
I don't like it here.

246
00:27:18,500 --> 00:27:21,470
Your pa's getting things in order.
When he does he'll send for you.

247
00:27:22,070 --> 00:27:23,370
It's been a year.

248
00:27:24,470 --> 00:27:25,870
Don't worry, he will.

249
00:27:27,810 --> 00:27:29,780
And your mom's buried here.

250
00:27:30,740 --> 00:27:32,370
You know I can't leave my little girl.

251
00:27:40,420 --> 00:27:42,550
- Taggart?
- Yeah, I see them.

252
00:27:43,420 --> 00:27:45,890
Emmett, you go inside. Now.

253
00:28:05,410 --> 00:28:07,470
I want my boy, John.

254
00:28:07,580 --> 00:28:08,710
Pa?

255
00:28:09,220 --> 00:28:10,610
Pa!

256
00:28:13,850 --> 00:28:15,340
I knew you'd come for me, Pa.

257
00:28:15,460 --> 00:28:17,620
Shut up! I'll deal with you later.

258
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:21,620
Yeah, that's Lonergan, boss.

259
00:28:26,700 --> 00:28:30,190
That's the son of a bitch
stole my gold off the bullion coach.

260
00:28:30,300 --> 00:28:31,670
I want that man.

261
00:28:31,770 --> 00:28:34,210
You're gonna have to take it up
with the judge in Santa Fe.

262
00:28:34,310 --> 00:28:36,070
I ain't going to Santa Fe.

263
00:28:36,180 --> 00:28:38,110
You give him to me now

264
00:28:38,210 --> 00:28:39,940
or I'm gonna take him.

265
00:28:40,050 --> 00:28:41,380
What about me, Pa?

266
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:43,140
I said, shut up, boy!

267
00:29:21,890 --> 00:29:23,450
What the hell is that?

268
00:29:43,380 --> 00:29:45,000
What the hell?

269
00:30:06,100 --> 00:30:07,070
Hey!

270
00:30:29,060 --> 00:30:30,550
- They're coming back!
- They're coming around again.

271
00:30:30,660 --> 00:30:32,280
They're coming back! Dismount!

272
00:30:44,670 --> 00:30:45,660
- Get out of the way!
- Maria!

273
00:30:46,070 --> 00:30:47,370
Oh, God!

274
00:30:47,870 --> 00:30:49,360
Don't move! Don't move!

275
00:30:49,480 --> 00:30:52,210
Stay there! Stay right there!
Don't move! I'm coming!

276
00:31:02,590 --> 00:31:04,020
Give me your hand.

277
00:31:04,120 --> 00:31:05,820
- Give me your hand.
- What the hell for?

278
00:31:05,930 --> 00:31:08,590
I can get us free.
Just give me your hand.

279
00:31:09,500 --> 00:31:10,790
Hold still.

280
00:31:20,240 --> 00:31:21,540
Emmett!

281
00:31:24,110 --> 00:31:25,100
Grandpa!

282
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:28,870
Emmett!

283
00:31:29,720 --> 00:31:31,180
Emmett, it's all right. I got you, son.

284
00:31:38,290 --> 00:31:40,320
- Give me your hand.
- No!

285
00:31:40,430 --> 00:31:42,450
Come on, kid. Give me your hand!

286
00:31:58,140 --> 00:31:59,700
What is that?

287
00:32:27,740 --> 00:32:30,570
Come on, get up, boss.
Come on, we got to get out of here.

288
00:32:30,980 --> 00:32:32,100
Where's Percy?

289
00:32:35,920 --> 00:32:37,010
Come on out of there!

290
00:32:38,020 --> 00:32:40,750
- I can't, Pa.
- You can't? Coward!

291
00:32:41,720 --> 00:32:44,850
He broke my fingers!

292
00:32:50,300 --> 00:32:51,420
Pa!

293
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:53,160
Pa!

294
00:32:55,470 --> 00:32:57,200
Let's go! We got to go!

295
00:32:59,140 --> 00:33:00,440
This way!

296
00:34:57,720 --> 00:35:00,660
- What is that thing?
- Why are you asking me?

297
00:35:00,760 --> 00:35:02,560
Because you shot it!

298
00:35:03,560 --> 00:35:05,000
With that thing.
Where'd you get that thing?

299
00:35:05,100 --> 00:35:07,360
I don't know.

300
00:35:08,400 --> 00:35:11,060
What do you mean, you don't know?

301
00:35:16,610 --> 00:35:18,630
What the hell is that?

302
00:35:20,580 --> 00:35:22,210
They took my wife.

303
00:35:26,250 --> 00:35:27,740
Hey.

304
00:35:27,850 --> 00:35:29,340
Is anyone in there?

305
00:35:30,760 --> 00:35:31,880
No.

306
00:35:31,990 --> 00:35:33,460
Is my wife in there?

307
00:35:33,560 --> 00:35:34,860
No!

308
00:35:34,960 --> 00:35:36,590
Is it dead?

309
00:35:46,070 --> 00:35:48,870
- Is it demons?
- Demons?

310
00:35:49,010 --> 00:35:52,000
I can't rightly say.
Sure does fit the description, but...

311
00:35:52,110 --> 00:35:54,100
Demons? What are you talking about?

312
00:35:54,210 --> 00:35:55,770
You talking about Bible stuff? Demons?

313
00:35:55,880 --> 00:35:58,180
- I'm not talking about anything.
- What the hell are you talking about?

314
00:35:58,280 --> 00:35:59,340
You got to calm down, Doc.

315
00:35:59,450 --> 00:36:00,440
- Calm down?
- You're scaring the boy.

316
00:36:00,550 --> 00:36:02,780
You're telling me a bunch of demons
took my wife.

317
00:36:02,890 --> 00:36:04,790
- I didn't say any such thing.
- Took our people!

318
00:36:04,890 --> 00:36:06,450
- Get a hold of yourself.
- You're telling me to calm down!

319
00:36:29,450 --> 00:36:31,250
Boss!

320
00:36:31,350 --> 00:36:33,010
Boss!

321
00:36:33,120 --> 00:36:34,680
It went this way.

322
00:36:38,390 --> 00:36:41,420
I don't know what it is, but it's bleeding.

323
00:36:43,900 --> 00:36:47,630
That's the same direction
those machines went with our kin.

324
00:36:48,130 --> 00:36:51,430
We ain't gonna be able to track it
in the dark.

325
00:36:52,810 --> 00:36:54,640
Round up the horses,
get some supplies!

326
00:36:54,740 --> 00:36:56,570
We'll set off at first light!

327
00:36:57,780 --> 00:36:58,900
You.

328
00:37:00,650 --> 00:37:02,610
You're going with us.

329
00:37:03,320 --> 00:37:08,280
I need that weapon. It's the only thing
that counts. And I figure you owe me.

330
00:37:09,920 --> 00:37:12,050
I don't see it that way.

331
00:38:22,760 --> 00:38:24,230
What do you want?

332
00:38:24,900 --> 00:38:26,560
What do you want?

333
00:38:27,670 --> 00:38:30,070
You come clean right now, or I'll kill you.

334
00:38:30,170 --> 00:38:34,200
They took my people, too.
I've been looking for them a long time.

335
00:38:35,070 --> 00:38:36,630
I know you can help me find them.

336
00:38:40,250 --> 00:38:42,150
You stay away from me.

337
00:38:52,760 --> 00:38:54,560
I can help you!

338
00:39:02,870 --> 00:39:04,700
It's heading north.

339
00:39:05,840 --> 00:39:07,970
Its tracks are still fresh.

340
00:39:20,690 --> 00:39:22,920
If it's all the same,
I'd like to ride along, too.

341
00:39:23,020 --> 00:39:24,350
Yes, ma'am.

342
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:28,650
Got a kid and a dog, why not a woman?

343
00:40:15,170 --> 00:40:16,540
You're back.

344
00:40:32,690 --> 00:40:33,990
What's that?

345
00:40:50,840 --> 00:40:52,540
You have to take it back.

346
00:40:52,850 --> 00:40:54,370
Like hell I will.

347
00:40:54,780 --> 00:40:56,080
That's blood money.

348
00:40:56,180 --> 00:40:58,910
- Well, I goddamned earned it.
- By robbing and killing.

349
00:40:59,020 --> 00:41:01,080
That's gonna get us what we need!

350
00:41:33,490 --> 00:41:34,950
- Jake!
- Stay there!

351
00:41:35,050 --> 00:41:36,250
Jake!

352
00:42:08,450 --> 00:42:10,320
Well, well, well.

353
00:42:10,420 --> 00:42:12,220
Look who's back.

354
00:42:12,730 --> 00:42:15,490
I see you, but I don't see my gold.

355
00:42:15,590 --> 00:42:18,690
Let's say we find those people first,

356
00:42:18,800 --> 00:42:20,960
and then you can take your best shot
at collecting.

357
00:42:21,070 --> 00:42:25,370
Maybe that reward on your head
would be a more attractive proposition.

358
00:42:25,470 --> 00:42:30,100
Or I could just shoot you in the chest
and cut that thing off your arm.

359
00:42:31,040 --> 00:42:34,480
You know, Doc,
I don't even know why we're doing this.

360
00:42:34,580 --> 00:42:36,570
You know they're all dead.

361
00:42:37,750 --> 00:42:40,950
Well, I think if they wanted to kill them,
I think they would have.

362
00:42:41,050 --> 00:42:45,080
Only if the boss is right
and they was roping them.

363
00:42:45,930 --> 00:42:47,420
Bet it's to eat them.

364
00:42:49,190 --> 00:42:51,960
If it was me, I'd start with your wife.

365
00:42:54,430 --> 00:42:57,100
You gonna be like this the whole trip?
'Cause if you are,

366
00:42:57,200 --> 00:43:00,000
we ain't gonna have
too many long conversations, are we?

367
00:43:00,110 --> 00:43:02,670
Why don't you sing a song
or something?

368
00:43:02,780 --> 00:43:05,400
Cook some beans.
Do something useful.

369
00:43:15,120 --> 00:43:17,320
Take some friendly advice?

370
00:43:18,560 --> 00:43:21,620
Get yourself a gun
and learn how to use it.

371
00:43:29,700 --> 00:43:31,830
The tracks are washed away.

372
00:44:01,730 --> 00:44:06,340
I don't know much about boats,
but I'd say that one's upside-down.

373
00:44:07,510 --> 00:44:11,670
We're 500 miles from any river
big enough to hold it.

374
00:44:11,780 --> 00:44:14,080
Well, let's get inside, get out of the rain!

375
00:44:14,180 --> 00:44:16,010
I'm not going anywhere near that thing.

376
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:18,580
Suit yourself. Sleep in the rain.

377
00:44:49,380 --> 00:44:51,470
You fixin' to say something?

378
00:44:52,850 --> 00:44:54,150
Maybe...

379
00:44:55,050 --> 00:44:57,450
Maybe we should have
called in the Army?

380
00:44:57,560 --> 00:45:00,050
I ain't gonna turn this over
to no West Pointers

381
00:45:00,160 --> 00:45:04,530
who got to get on the telegraph to ask
Washington which hand to wipe with.

382
00:45:04,630 --> 00:45:08,230
I waited around at Antietam
for 'em to tell me what to do.

383
00:45:10,140 --> 00:45:12,760
And lost 328 men

384
00:45:13,570 --> 00:45:15,370
over a cornfield.

385
00:45:16,910 --> 00:45:19,210
I remember those stories.

386
00:45:22,250 --> 00:45:25,050
I don't recollect telling you any stories.

387
00:45:25,980 --> 00:45:29,940
I'd listen when you'd tell them to Percy.

388
00:45:30,790 --> 00:45:34,420
You get this through
your thick Indian skull.

389
00:45:36,800 --> 00:45:39,200
Them stories weren't for you.

390
00:45:41,900 --> 00:45:43,930
They were for my son.

391
00:45:47,340 --> 00:45:52,540
Get out of here.
Go look after the horses. Do your job.

392
00:46:31,680 --> 00:46:34,620
You've been looking at this knife.
You like this knife?

393
00:46:48,370 --> 00:46:50,160
You look after that.

394
00:46:52,370 --> 00:46:53,670
Don't lose it.

395
00:47:02,710 --> 00:47:05,620
Don't yank on it, it's not your pecker.
Now, here.

396
00:47:05,720 --> 00:47:08,620
You're holding onto this thing
like you're hanging from it.

397
00:47:13,390 --> 00:47:15,520
What the hell am I doing?

398
00:47:17,960 --> 00:47:19,660
It's my fault she got took.

399
00:47:19,770 --> 00:47:21,430
I never should have
taken her to that town.

400
00:47:21,570 --> 00:47:23,500
No, no, no. Not your fault.

401
00:47:23,600 --> 00:47:26,040
You'll get her back.
You're setting things right.

402
00:47:26,140 --> 00:47:27,870
Just got to have faith. That's all.

403
00:47:27,970 --> 00:47:31,700
Faith. Yeah.
God's been real swell to me.

404
00:47:31,810 --> 00:47:33,470
I don't mean no disrespect, preacher,

405
00:47:33,580 --> 00:47:37,110
but either he ain't up there,
or he don't like me very much.

406
00:47:37,220 --> 00:47:40,950
Surely you don't expect the Lord
to do everything for you, do you, Doc?

407
00:47:42,490 --> 00:47:44,890
You got to earn his presence.

408
00:47:44,990 --> 00:47:48,550
Then you got to recognize it,
and then you have to act on it.

409
00:47:50,430 --> 00:47:51,900
Now, keep your eye on the target.

410
00:47:54,170 --> 00:47:55,460
And shoot.

411
00:48:01,670 --> 00:48:05,400
That's better. Better.
Come on. Let's reload.

412
00:48:27,370 --> 00:48:29,160
You been there long?

413
00:48:29,670 --> 00:48:30,970
Yes.

414
00:48:41,880 --> 00:48:43,510
There something you need?

415
00:48:44,380 --> 00:48:45,850
Who is she?

416
00:48:49,220 --> 00:48:51,620
She's the only one who knows who I am.

417
00:48:51,720 --> 00:48:53,850
No, you know who you are.

418
00:48:54,560 --> 00:48:57,190
- You just have to remember.
- Well, I can't.

419
00:48:57,300 --> 00:48:58,920
Yes, you can.

420
00:49:14,580 --> 00:49:16,050
Does it hurt?

421
00:49:19,580 --> 00:49:21,280
It's fine.

422
00:49:28,930 --> 00:49:30,050
It's here.

423
00:50:08,600 --> 00:50:10,860
Easy, hey! Easy!

424
00:50:10,970 --> 00:50:12,370
What's wrong, boy?

425
00:50:13,110 --> 00:50:14,570
Hello?

426
00:51:42,090 --> 00:51:43,860
Get away from that boy!

427
00:51:48,100 --> 00:51:49,070
No!

428
00:52:17,430 --> 00:52:20,960
- The boy. The boy.
- He's fine. He's fine.

429
00:52:21,730 --> 00:52:23,530
It's okay. It's okay.

430
00:52:27,310 --> 00:52:29,930
You go get our people back.

431
00:52:31,980 --> 00:52:34,500
God don't care who you were, son.

432
00:52:35,080 --> 00:52:37,140
Only who you are.

433
00:53:06,680 --> 00:53:07,980
Dog?

434
00:53:09,280 --> 00:53:10,370
Come on, boy!

435
00:53:12,780 --> 00:53:14,480
Where are you?

436
00:53:16,450 --> 00:53:19,790
Tracks are good. It's headed north.
Where's the men?

437
00:53:19,890 --> 00:53:22,620
They run off. Goddamn cowards.

438
00:53:22,730 --> 00:53:24,290
I can't find the dog.

439
00:53:24,400 --> 00:53:28,060
We ain't waiting for him.
He's run off or dead. Let's go.

440
00:53:28,170 --> 00:53:29,360
Hey. Hey. Wait.

441
00:53:29,470 --> 00:53:31,960
Aren't we gonna
say some words over him?

442
00:53:32,070 --> 00:53:35,130
Only one who knows what to say
is in the ground.

443
00:53:35,240 --> 00:53:37,640
Ain't it enough we took the time
to put him there?

444
00:53:37,740 --> 00:53:39,940
No. No, it's not enough.

445
00:53:51,860 --> 00:53:53,480
You go ahead.

446
00:53:57,860 --> 00:53:59,160
Lord...

447
00:54:02,200 --> 00:54:06,190
If there is such a thing as a soul
this man had a good one.

448
00:54:06,340 --> 00:54:07,430
Please protect it.

449
00:54:08,170 --> 00:54:09,800
Made me feel better.

450
00:54:09,910 --> 00:54:12,270
World was a better place
for having him.

451
00:54:12,380 --> 00:54:15,040
Dust to dust, amen. How was that?

452
00:54:15,150 --> 00:54:16,550
Good words.

453
00:54:27,230 --> 00:54:29,660
What are you all choked up about?

454
00:54:31,560 --> 00:54:33,960
I'm worried about my grandpa.

455
00:54:38,900 --> 00:54:43,310
Look. When I was only just
a little bit older than you are now

456
00:54:43,410 --> 00:54:45,540
all this was Mexico.

457
00:54:47,110 --> 00:54:52,410
Word come that the Apaches was riding
towards a settlement called Arivaca.

458
00:54:54,520 --> 00:54:56,380
My father wanted me to be a man,

459
00:54:56,490 --> 00:55:00,250
so he made me ride out with
the garrison, banging on a drum.

460
00:55:02,690 --> 00:55:04,660
Boy, was I scared.

461
00:55:07,530 --> 00:55:10,130
Well, we got there, it was too late.
They were all dead,

462
00:55:10,240 --> 00:55:12,430
the place was all burnt down.

463
00:55:13,410 --> 00:55:15,700
This one settler fella

464
00:55:16,570 --> 00:55:19,540
came crawling out of a burning cabin.

465
00:55:21,250 --> 00:55:22,710
He was bad.

466
00:55:23,680 --> 00:55:25,780
He knew he was gonna die.

467
00:55:26,920 --> 00:55:28,650
Burnt bad.

468
00:55:31,020 --> 00:55:32,650
He rolled over,

469
00:55:33,630 --> 00:55:35,750
looked up into my eyes,

470
00:55:37,100 --> 00:55:39,390
and he said, "Kill me."

471
00:55:42,270 --> 00:55:43,930
What did you do?

472
00:55:49,270 --> 00:55:51,870
I took this knife off his belt

473
00:55:52,610 --> 00:55:54,580
and I slit his throat.

474
00:55:57,050 --> 00:55:58,350
Take it.

475
00:56:02,120 --> 00:56:03,710
Be a man.

476
00:56:12,800 --> 00:56:15,100
That's a little rough, isn't it?

477
00:56:15,900 --> 00:56:17,530
He means well.

478
00:56:32,250 --> 00:56:35,810
I got him.
The tracks are closer together.

479
00:56:35,920 --> 00:56:37,850
He's slowing down,
headed to that canyon.

480
00:56:59,940 --> 00:57:02,170
Put your hands up in the air!

481
00:57:04,780 --> 00:57:07,340
That means you, too, pretty lady.

482
00:57:09,220 --> 00:57:11,620
This is what they call a hold-up.

483
00:57:11,720 --> 00:57:15,250
Welcome, everybody. Welcome.

484
00:57:19,300 --> 00:57:20,360
Boss?

485
00:57:21,970 --> 00:57:23,590
Boss, is that you?

486
00:57:25,140 --> 00:57:26,730
Lonergan?

487
00:57:27,140 --> 00:57:29,700
What in the hell are you doing here?

488
00:57:33,480 --> 00:57:36,210
Who are your amigos?

489
00:57:38,480 --> 00:57:40,880
Is this your new gang, Jake?

490
00:57:44,490 --> 00:57:47,050
I never thought I'd see you again, Jake.

491
00:57:49,990 --> 00:57:51,590
You were always my favorite.

492
00:57:52,630 --> 00:57:53,820
Shut up.

493
00:57:56,070 --> 00:57:57,300
Damn it.

494
00:57:57,400 --> 00:58:00,240
Jake? Did you break my tooth?

495
00:58:00,340 --> 00:58:02,640
Would you shut up? I'm thinking.

496
00:58:06,240 --> 00:58:08,410
How many boys we got left?

497
00:58:09,750 --> 00:58:11,180
About the same.

498
00:58:12,820 --> 00:58:14,220
Which is?

499
00:58:15,450 --> 00:58:16,610
Thirty?

500
00:58:17,360 --> 00:58:19,650
That's right. Thirty.

501
00:58:20,160 --> 00:58:21,250
Good.

502
00:58:23,360 --> 00:58:25,060
- That's good.
- Yeah.

503
00:58:26,360 --> 00:58:28,260
You're gonna bring me to the camp.

504
00:58:30,700 --> 00:58:32,690
It's time to set things straight.

505
00:58:35,040 --> 00:58:37,270
We're gonna go to the camp!

506
00:58:37,710 --> 00:58:39,180
How's the haul?

507
00:58:39,280 --> 00:58:42,540
Vulture Mine gold. Looking pretty rich.

508
00:58:42,650 --> 00:58:46,110
- How much dynamite we get?
- We got 50 sticks or so.

509
00:58:46,220 --> 00:58:47,880
Dolan!

510
00:58:51,290 --> 00:58:53,520
About time you got back.

511
00:58:53,630 --> 00:58:55,150
What the hell happened to you?

512
00:58:55,790 --> 00:58:57,090
He did.

513
00:59:04,600 --> 00:59:06,330
Well, shit.

514
00:59:10,340 --> 00:59:12,140
You got some balls

515
00:59:12,240 --> 00:59:15,370
riding back in here
like nothing ever happened.

516
00:59:16,450 --> 00:59:20,510
Boys! Grab your guns. We're riding out.

517
00:59:21,050 --> 00:59:23,020
Boys aren't going anywhere with you,
Jake.

518
00:59:24,960 --> 00:59:27,690
We're fixing to rob us a coach.

519
00:59:27,790 --> 00:59:29,420
And that's exactly what we're gonna do.

520
00:59:37,390 --> 00:59:39,160
Are you her?

521
00:59:39,960 --> 00:59:41,400
Am I who?

522
00:59:41,500 --> 00:59:44,230
The whore that Jake quit this gang for.

523
00:59:45,770 --> 00:59:47,000
You watch your mouth.

524
00:59:47,100 --> 00:59:48,400
Or what?

525
00:59:49,400 --> 00:59:52,130
I run this outfit now.

526
00:59:52,240 --> 00:59:53,670
Put your guns on the whore!

527
00:59:53,780 --> 00:59:57,730
If he so much as twitches,
blow her brains out of her ear.

528
01:00:01,150 --> 01:00:03,120
He said the whore.

529
01:00:04,750 --> 01:00:08,480
You call her a whore again,
it'll be the last word you ever say.

530
01:00:08,590 --> 01:00:11,890
You ain't in no position
to make threats, boyo.

531
01:00:11,990 --> 01:00:13,790
Hunt, take his gun.

532
01:00:14,760 --> 01:00:16,290
Take his gun!

533
01:00:18,000 --> 01:00:19,630
Sorry, Jake.

534
01:00:39,150 --> 01:00:41,180
Where's our gold, Jake?

535
01:00:42,490 --> 01:00:44,150
I don't remember.

536
01:00:52,200 --> 01:00:54,100
Well, I do remember

537
01:00:54,200 --> 01:00:58,500
you telling us you was leaving us
high and dry because of some woman.

538
01:01:09,520 --> 01:01:14,790
I guess you just left out the part about
taking all of our gold from that last job?

539
01:01:16,330 --> 01:01:18,790
So I'm gonna ask you one last time.

540
01:01:19,730 --> 01:01:21,820
Where is it, Jake?

541
01:01:24,170 --> 01:01:25,460
Demons.

542
01:01:28,570 --> 01:01:29,660
What's that?

543
01:01:30,240 --> 01:01:32,210
Demons took your gold.

544
01:01:33,410 --> 01:01:35,380
When you get to hell

545
01:01:36,580 --> 01:01:38,640
you can ask for it back.

546
01:01:47,760 --> 01:01:49,380
Kill the whore.

547
01:02:02,870 --> 01:02:05,600
I told you not to call her that.

548
01:02:05,710 --> 01:02:07,540
Everybody!

549
01:02:07,640 --> 01:02:08,940
Drop 'em!

550
01:02:10,180 --> 01:02:11,480
I said drop 'em!

551
01:02:19,120 --> 01:02:20,590
Not fun, is it?

552
01:02:21,120 --> 01:02:23,720
You know, that wasn't very nice.

553
01:02:27,960 --> 01:02:29,120
On your horses!

554
01:02:29,800 --> 01:02:30,860
Go!

555
01:02:32,030 --> 01:02:35,160
Jake, Jake, Jake. Don't forget your gun.

556
01:02:35,270 --> 01:02:36,530
You'll always be my favorite.

557
01:02:46,350 --> 01:02:48,440
- Mount up!
- Ride!

558
01:03:17,580 --> 01:03:19,740
- They're here!
- Move out!

559
01:03:39,200 --> 01:03:40,500
Come on!

560
01:04:51,770 --> 01:04:52,970
Okay. I got you!

561
01:04:53,070 --> 01:04:54,170
I got you!

562
01:05:09,960 --> 01:05:11,430
Can you swim?

563
01:05:16,700 --> 01:05:17,960
Oh, God.

564
01:05:18,070 --> 01:05:19,160
Turn your head!

565
01:05:44,490 --> 01:05:46,050
You all right?

566
01:05:51,030 --> 01:05:52,550
Let's get in.

567
01:06:12,220 --> 01:06:13,840
We were flying.

568
01:06:15,150 --> 01:06:16,710
Yeah!

569
01:06:17,120 --> 01:06:18,950
I don't want to do that again.

570
01:06:19,060 --> 01:06:20,180
No.

571
01:07:32,830 --> 01:07:34,020
Hey.

572
01:07:34,860 --> 01:07:36,730
Hey, you stay with me.

573
01:07:38,030 --> 01:07:39,500
Keep talking.

574
01:07:41,000 --> 01:07:43,230
You remember now, don't you?

575
01:07:44,710 --> 01:07:45,830
What?

576
01:07:46,540 --> 01:07:47,840
The woman.

577
01:07:49,550 --> 01:07:51,340
Did you love her?

578
01:07:52,880 --> 01:07:54,780
You can tell me.

579
01:07:54,880 --> 01:07:56,880
I can't remember.

580
01:07:57,550 --> 01:07:59,020
I must've.

581
01:07:59,960 --> 01:08:02,250
All I know is I owe it to her

582
01:08:03,430 --> 01:08:04,890
to find her.

583
01:08:07,260 --> 01:08:09,820
Watch out. I'm sorry.

584
01:08:09,930 --> 01:08:11,230
I'm sorry.

585
01:08:12,770 --> 01:08:14,130
I got you.

586
01:08:15,100 --> 01:08:16,570
I got you.

587
01:08:20,940 --> 01:08:22,570
It's not far now.

588
01:08:24,710 --> 01:08:26,010
You and me,

589
01:08:27,450 --> 01:08:29,250
we're gonna be just fine.

590
01:08:36,990 --> 01:08:37,960
Is that...

591
01:08:38,530 --> 01:08:39,990
Is that them?

592
01:08:40,800 --> 01:08:41,920
Boss?

593
01:08:51,810 --> 01:08:55,040
- I got her.
- Give her to me, Nat. Bring her here.

594
01:08:59,080 --> 01:09:02,950
- Here. Drink.
- No. Give it to her. Give it to her.

595
01:09:13,560 --> 01:09:15,360
Doc?

596
01:09:26,340 --> 01:09:27,830
How is she?

597
01:09:30,350 --> 01:09:32,140
She's gone, pal.

598
01:09:32,250 --> 01:09:36,810
No. No, she's not gone.

599
01:09:36,920 --> 01:09:39,010
She's not. She's not gone!

600
01:09:40,020 --> 01:09:41,320
Jake.

601
01:09:42,590 --> 01:09:44,290
She's gone.

602
01:10:18,890 --> 01:10:20,690
- Doc!
- Don't touch him!

603
01:10:21,160 --> 01:10:22,430
Doc!

604
01:10:58,100 --> 01:10:59,590
This is Black Knife.

605
01:11:01,700 --> 01:11:02,860
The last of his people.

606
01:11:02,970 --> 01:11:05,910
There's no reasoning with them.
We're all gonna die anyway.

607
01:11:06,010 --> 01:11:07,810
This is what's left of the Chiricahuas.

608
01:11:07,910 --> 01:11:09,040
Good riddance to 'em!

609
01:11:10,280 --> 01:11:12,340
He's saying the white people,

610
01:11:12,450 --> 01:11:14,280
they brought all this evil to his people.

611
01:11:14,380 --> 01:11:18,010
We brought evil? Evil was here!
You're the evil one!

612
01:11:18,150 --> 01:11:20,520
He's saying we brought the monsters.

613
01:11:20,660 --> 01:11:23,450
We didn't bring the monsters.
Tell him they took our people, too!

614
01:11:23,560 --> 01:11:24,990
Tell him they took my wife!

615
01:11:25,090 --> 01:11:27,530
Shut up!
There's no reasoning with them!

616
01:11:28,160 --> 01:11:29,690
Tell him what I said, Nat!

617
01:11:29,900 --> 01:11:31,160
Kill us now!

618
01:12:36,830 --> 01:12:39,630
I'm sorry, but I couldn't tell you.

619
01:12:39,740 --> 01:12:41,260
Are you one of them?

620
01:12:41,370 --> 01:12:44,860
No. I'm from a different place.

621
01:12:44,970 --> 01:12:48,030
I took this form
so I could walk among you.

622
01:12:49,380 --> 01:12:50,900
You should have told me.

623
01:12:51,010 --> 01:12:53,610
I didn't know if I could heal this body,

624
01:12:53,720 --> 01:12:55,450
if I would wake up.

625
01:13:07,300 --> 01:13:09,790
He wants to know where you're from.

626
01:13:19,610 --> 01:13:20,700
What'd she say?

627
01:13:20,810 --> 01:13:24,140
She says she came from a place
above the stars.

628
01:13:24,610 --> 01:13:26,910
What does that mean? Another world?
What do you mean?

629
01:13:27,020 --> 01:13:28,980
What does that mean? What?

630
01:13:29,290 --> 01:13:31,080
He says you shouldn't talk.

631
01:13:31,190 --> 01:13:32,710
What do you mean I shouldn't talk?
I got questions...

632
01:13:33,820 --> 01:13:35,190
You're a guest of the chief.

633
01:13:35,290 --> 01:13:38,090
Now I'm a guest? I thought
I was a prisoner! What the hell am I?

634
01:13:38,190 --> 01:13:40,860
Enough! All right. You're both big men!
Great warriors!

635
01:13:40,960 --> 01:13:43,450
Can we just listen to the woman
tell her story?

636
01:13:43,570 --> 01:13:45,290
Or whatever she is?
What are they doing here?

637
01:13:45,670 --> 01:13:47,190
They want gold.

638
01:13:49,610 --> 01:13:51,100
Well, that's just ridiculous.

639
01:13:51,210 --> 01:13:53,330
What are they gonna do,
buy something?

640
01:13:53,440 --> 01:13:56,140
It's as rare to them as it is to you.

641
01:13:56,250 --> 01:13:57,340
What about my grandpa?

642
01:13:57,450 --> 01:14:01,710
What about my wife? What about
the other people? Are they still alive?

643
01:14:01,820 --> 01:14:03,810
If they are, they won't be for long.

644
01:14:05,920 --> 01:14:08,220
They're studying your weaknesses.

645
01:14:08,320 --> 01:14:10,290
These are just scouts.

646
01:14:10,390 --> 01:14:15,490
If we let them leave, they'll come back
with more and there will be no survivors.

647
01:14:15,600 --> 01:14:17,720
That's what they did to my people.

648
01:14:17,830 --> 01:14:20,460
I came here to make sure
it would not happen again,

649
01:14:20,570 --> 01:14:23,090
but we have to work together.

650
01:14:29,240 --> 01:14:31,470
He says his people will join her.

651
01:14:32,180 --> 01:14:33,150
What do you mean, join her?

652
01:14:33,250 --> 01:14:35,150
What's she going to do?
Where you going to go?

653
01:14:35,250 --> 01:14:37,120
We can find them.
He knows where they are.

654
01:14:41,590 --> 01:14:42,680
No, I don't.

655
01:14:44,360 --> 01:14:47,230
I can't remember anything.
I couldn't even remember my own name.

656
01:14:51,030 --> 01:14:53,760
He says they will take care of that.

657
01:17:18,750 --> 01:17:20,540
I brought the gold.

658
01:17:21,820 --> 01:17:23,150
Into the house.

659
01:17:24,920 --> 01:17:27,180
That's why she died.

660
01:17:27,960 --> 01:17:30,150
It's not your fault.

661
01:18:39,860 --> 01:18:41,760
I know where they are.

662
01:19:28,140 --> 01:19:30,270
Jesus, Mary and Joseph.

663
01:19:32,210 --> 01:19:34,270
How did they build something like that?

664
01:19:34,420 --> 01:19:37,210
They arrived in it. It's their vessel.

665
01:19:37,720 --> 01:19:40,020
That's only the top.
The rest is underground.

666
01:19:40,120 --> 01:19:41,350
It's how they mine for gold.

667
01:19:41,460 --> 01:19:43,080
So there is gold here.

668
01:19:44,230 --> 01:19:45,750
Can they see out of there?

669
01:19:46,230 --> 01:19:47,890
They don't see well in daylight.

670
01:19:48,000 --> 01:19:50,730
They stay underground in caverns
where it's dark.

671
01:20:21,330 --> 01:20:22,960
We'll never even get close.

672
01:20:23,100 --> 01:20:25,030
Those flying machines
will just pick us off

673
01:20:25,130 --> 01:20:26,500
before we get anywhere near it.

674
01:20:26,600 --> 01:20:28,470
There is another way in.

675
01:20:29,270 --> 01:20:30,740
Down there.

676
01:20:31,510 --> 01:20:32,940
The way I came out.

677
01:20:34,840 --> 01:20:36,610
We got to get those creatures
out of there

678
01:20:36,710 --> 01:20:40,080
and out in the open,
where we can get at them.

679
01:20:40,180 --> 01:20:43,350
So you can get in with that arm gun,
get our people out.

680
01:20:45,290 --> 01:20:48,420
We have one advantage,
they underestimate you.

681
01:20:48,520 --> 01:20:50,420
You're like insects to them.

682
01:20:50,530 --> 01:20:53,320
They're not planning on defending
themselves, so they'll be vulnerable.

683
01:20:54,630 --> 01:20:58,190
- We haven't got enough men.
- This ain't gonna work.

684
01:21:02,740 --> 01:21:05,710
He says he wants to use your spyglass.

685
01:21:31,930 --> 01:21:34,830
The Apaches are mountain warriors.

686
01:21:34,940 --> 01:21:38,740
He says it's better to fight
from high ground.

687
01:21:39,940 --> 01:21:41,370
Tell him he's a fool.

688
01:21:41,480 --> 01:21:44,450
There is no high ground
while they got those flying machines.

689
01:21:44,950 --> 01:21:46,210
Jake's leaving!

690
01:21:53,920 --> 01:21:55,360
That's just dandy.

691
01:21:55,490 --> 01:21:57,620
Son of a bitch.

692
01:22:00,560 --> 01:22:02,500
Quit stalling.
How much gold we had left?

693
01:22:02,600 --> 01:22:05,160
Barely enough.
But I'm gonna need my share right now

694
01:22:05,270 --> 01:22:07,670
so I can get as far away from here
as I possibly can.

695
01:22:10,740 --> 01:22:13,540
- Red?
- I got him, Bull.

696
01:22:15,710 --> 01:22:17,340
Hey, there.

697
01:22:19,950 --> 01:22:22,940
I had one hell of a job finding you boys.

698
01:22:24,620 --> 01:22:26,520
You planning a trip?

699
01:22:29,460 --> 01:22:31,590
We're going as far away as we can go.

700
01:22:31,690 --> 01:22:33,630
You remember la playa
in Puerto Vallarta?

701
01:22:33,730 --> 01:22:35,320
They got good fishing.

702
01:22:36,060 --> 01:22:38,620
Good tequila.
You want to come with us?

703
01:22:38,730 --> 01:22:40,930
Don't make no difference.

704
01:22:42,140 --> 01:22:43,870
It's not far enough.

705
01:22:45,970 --> 01:22:48,240
What in the hell
were those things, Jake?

706
01:22:48,340 --> 01:22:50,040
It doesn't matter.

707
01:22:50,150 --> 01:22:54,280
They're gonna find us
and they're gonna wipe us out.

708
01:22:55,080 --> 01:22:57,180
What in the hell are you saying?

709
01:22:58,090 --> 01:23:00,680
What I'm saying is you got a choice.

710
01:23:01,490 --> 01:23:04,320
You can drink your last few hours away
on a beach,

711
01:23:04,430 --> 01:23:07,590
which by the way, is not a bad idea

712
01:23:09,060 --> 01:23:11,860
or you can follow me one last time.

713
01:23:22,310 --> 01:23:25,440
We got to make the best use
of our resources.

714
01:23:25,550 --> 01:23:29,240
We got to have a strict...
Listen to me, damn it!

715
01:23:29,820 --> 01:23:33,080
He doesn't understand tactics.
You got to explain to him.

716
01:23:33,190 --> 01:23:36,520
Look, we can't just run around hollering

717
01:23:36,630 --> 01:23:39,920
and throwing spears and
shooting arrows at the damn thing.

718
01:23:40,030 --> 01:23:44,160
We got to draw them out of there
onto open ground

719
01:23:44,270 --> 01:23:47,670
where we can surround them,
attack them on all sides.

720
01:23:47,770 --> 01:23:49,900
Flank them. Explain to him.

721
01:23:53,510 --> 01:23:56,810
He said he's not going to let you
lead his people.

722
01:24:06,960 --> 01:24:08,650
What's he saying?

723
01:24:10,330 --> 01:24:12,350
He's saying they need to
open their hearts

724
01:24:12,460 --> 01:24:15,760
and see in you what he has seen.

725
01:24:20,040 --> 01:24:22,830
That his parents
died in the Mexican War

726
01:24:23,540 --> 01:24:26,300
and you took him in
when he was only a boy.

727
01:24:29,080 --> 01:24:31,170
That you gave him purpose.

728
01:24:31,980 --> 01:24:36,540
Taught him how to take care of himself
even though you were not blood.

729
01:24:41,560 --> 01:24:45,860
That you despise battle
but would never run from it.

730
01:24:47,960 --> 01:24:51,690
That you're a fierce warrior
worthy of any fight.

731
01:25:10,850 --> 01:25:12,290
He says if you're such a great warrior,

732
01:25:12,390 --> 01:25:15,290
why do you only have a man and a boy
to follow you into battle?

733
01:25:50,730 --> 01:25:53,560
Dog! Dog!

734
01:25:55,400 --> 01:25:56,690
Boy!

735
01:25:56,800 --> 01:25:58,100
How are you?

736
01:26:09,980 --> 01:26:12,210
Hot damn.

737
01:26:12,780 --> 01:26:15,050
Ready to get your son back?

738
01:27:38,070 --> 01:27:40,130
Give me that. Okay.

739
01:27:48,410 --> 01:27:49,880
Matches.

740
01:28:01,060 --> 01:28:03,820
I don't have any more matches.
We're gonna have to go down.

741
01:28:03,930 --> 01:28:05,290
I don't know what we're going to do.

742
01:28:12,930 --> 01:28:14,990
Go. Go!

743
01:28:28,480 --> 01:28:29,640
Go. Go!

744
01:29:09,690 --> 01:29:11,420
I think we destroyed it.

745
01:29:23,740 --> 01:29:25,670
Demons are coming out.

746
01:29:29,540 --> 01:29:31,710
Take this. Go up where I showed you.

747
01:29:31,810 --> 01:29:33,540
- You see our people, wave your arms.
- Yes, sir.

748
01:29:33,650 --> 01:29:35,550
Move out!

749
01:29:48,930 --> 01:29:50,330
Good job.

750
01:29:50,430 --> 01:29:53,760
If our people are in there,
I'll get them out.

751
01:29:53,870 --> 01:29:55,100
Godspeed.

752
01:29:56,570 --> 01:29:57,870
Let's get them!

753
01:31:11,050 --> 01:31:13,640
This is how they get the gold out.

754
01:31:37,970 --> 01:31:39,410
They're not going down!

755
01:31:39,510 --> 01:31:42,940
They will!
Keep at it till we get our people out!

756
01:32:44,940 --> 01:32:46,070
Doc!

757
01:32:46,810 --> 01:32:48,440
Doc, get down here!

758
01:32:51,610 --> 01:32:52,740
Jesus.

759
01:32:55,620 --> 01:32:56,740
Doc!

760
01:32:58,050 --> 01:32:59,580
Did we get one?

761
01:33:01,360 --> 01:33:03,020
Yeah, we got one.

762
01:33:04,860 --> 01:33:09,590
I always dreamed of riding into battle
with you.

763
01:33:12,630 --> 01:33:15,660
I always dreamed
of having a son like you.

764
01:33:19,270 --> 01:33:20,330
Go.

765
01:33:21,110 --> 01:33:22,410
Get Percy.

766
01:33:23,310 --> 01:33:24,780
Get your son.

767
01:34:53,630 --> 01:34:55,190
Don't look into the light.

768
01:35:31,040 --> 01:35:33,670
- I told you not to look into the light.
- Yeah, right.

769
01:35:53,430 --> 01:35:55,190
How long are they gonna be like this?

770
01:35:55,300 --> 01:35:57,090
Each one's different.

771
01:36:02,040 --> 01:36:03,090
Hold them off.

772
01:36:03,200 --> 01:36:05,100
You'd better hurry.

773
01:36:45,750 --> 01:36:48,210
There's more of them coming!

774
01:37:23,020 --> 01:37:24,310
Go!

775
01:37:48,810 --> 01:37:50,330
Everybody's out.

776
01:37:50,980 --> 01:37:52,310
Right.

777
01:37:53,710 --> 01:37:56,180
Hey! Where are you going?

778
01:37:56,750 --> 01:37:59,350
It's this way!

779
01:38:48,570 --> 01:38:49,660
Go. Go!

780
01:40:25,570 --> 01:40:27,690
What the hell are you doing?
We have to get out of here!

781
01:40:27,800 --> 01:40:29,000
No!

782
01:40:29,600 --> 01:40:31,630
I came here to destroy that thing.

783
01:40:31,740 --> 01:40:32,730
How?

784
01:40:32,840 --> 01:40:34,930
With the bracelet. Take it off.

785
01:40:35,280 --> 01:40:37,010
Wait, I can't take it off.

786
01:40:37,110 --> 01:40:38,740
Yes, you can. You can control it.

787
01:40:38,850 --> 01:40:41,440
- How?
- Same way you shoot it. With your mind.

788
01:40:42,980 --> 01:40:45,140
You have to stop thinking.

789
01:40:56,230 --> 01:40:57,530
This isn't working.

790
01:41:13,310 --> 01:41:14,780
It fell off.

791
01:41:24,330 --> 01:41:27,450
If I can get it to its core, I can stop them.

792
01:41:30,100 --> 01:41:32,090
Let's go.

793
01:41:43,180 --> 01:41:44,470
Take this.

794
01:42:10,700 --> 01:42:11,860
Throw it!

795
01:42:17,080 --> 01:42:19,070
- Good-bye, Jake.
- What?

796
01:42:20,510 --> 01:42:22,710
Wait! Ella!

797
01:42:24,490 --> 01:42:25,710
No!

798
01:43:25,910 --> 01:43:27,900
I see them! I see them!

799
01:43:28,020 --> 01:43:29,950
They got out.
They're coming out the other side!

800
01:43:30,050 --> 01:43:31,210
You see Percy?

801
01:43:35,390 --> 01:43:36,380
Yeah, I see him!

802
01:43:36,490 --> 01:43:37,980
What about Jake and Ella?

803
01:43:38,560 --> 01:43:40,690
No. They're not there.

804
01:46:39,870 --> 01:46:41,470
You all right, old man?

805
01:46:51,080 --> 01:46:54,020
- Where's the girl?
- She's still inside.

806
01:47:00,160 --> 01:47:01,290
Go!

807
01:49:25,440 --> 01:49:26,500
Grandpa!

808
01:49:27,540 --> 01:49:28,840
It's me.

809
01:49:30,840 --> 01:49:31,970
Emmett.

810
01:49:32,080 --> 01:49:33,380
Emmett.

811
01:49:39,450 --> 01:49:41,250
You're all grown up.

812
01:49:48,960 --> 01:49:50,490
Percy.

813
01:49:55,270 --> 01:49:57,500
Don't you remember me, boy?

814
01:49:58,440 --> 01:50:02,640
I'm sorry. I don't remember much.

815
01:50:03,480 --> 01:50:05,100
I'm your father.

816
01:50:06,550 --> 01:50:08,070
Pa.

817
01:50:18,430 --> 01:50:20,790
Do you remember me?

818
01:50:34,070 --> 01:50:37,740
I thought you were dead.
I thought you were dead.

819
01:52:20,010 --> 01:52:23,040
All this gold's
gonna make things different.

820
01:52:23,480 --> 01:52:27,210
We're gonna have
a railroad in here soon.

821
01:52:27,320 --> 01:52:29,910
That'll change the cattle business.

822
01:52:32,160 --> 01:52:35,360
Run these ledgers
back to the bank for me, will you?

823
01:52:35,460 --> 01:52:37,860
Tell them I need some new checks.

824
01:52:38,770 --> 01:52:39,860
Okay.

825
01:52:41,870 --> 01:52:45,960
I want the new ones to read
"Dolarhyde and Son."

826
01:52:48,980 --> 01:52:53,110
- That sound good to you?
- Yes. Yes, sir.

827
01:53:04,990 --> 01:53:07,860
- John.
- Woodrow.

828
01:53:09,300 --> 01:53:12,860
It appears our town
is about to get a whole lot bigger.

829
01:53:18,040 --> 01:53:20,630
You weren't gonna leave
without saying good-bye, were you?

830
01:53:24,440 --> 01:53:26,210
I'm a wanted man.

831
01:53:27,150 --> 01:53:30,740
I could have sworn I saw
Jake Lonergan die in those caves,

832
01:53:30,850 --> 01:53:32,280
didn't you, Sheriff?

833
01:53:32,390 --> 01:53:34,010
Damn shame.

834
01:53:34,120 --> 01:53:36,350
I was looking forward
to hanging him myself.

835
01:53:38,330 --> 01:53:40,050
I could use a good man around here.

836
01:53:40,160 --> 01:53:41,960
Yes, you could.

837
01:53:47,400 --> 01:53:48,630
Jake.

838
01:53:50,970 --> 01:53:53,000
She's in a better place.

839
01:53:56,810 --> 01:53:58,330
I'll see you around, Colonel.
